 I have only completed Nethack twice - once with a barbarian (version 2)
and with a samurai (version 3.1.3). IMHO I could never have done it
without backing up my save games. Imagine this - say I had fluked out and
gotten my Samurai down to the wizard, done the ceremony then gotten the
amulet. The fact that it likes to teleport me down levels every so often
is one of the cruelest jokes I have ever seen. I once had it done twice in
a row and descended about 4 or 5 levels as a result. Also there are the
constant group of monsters who suddenly appear around you. This was
compounded by the Wizard of Yendor who had disintegrated nearly all my
armour leaving me facing a hoard of monsters buck naked. Then after I
managed to struggle up through the levels and after a few goes complete
the elemental planes I found myself in the Astral plane. Wandering into a
room I met Death who I pounded a few times till he went down. Now I knew
at the time it may have been a stupid idea but I decided to eat Death.
Result : foolishly ate Death in the endgame.
 Add to this the two times I stored a wand of cancellation in my bag of
holding, the eel who I didn't know could drown me, the fact that praying in
the levels sacred to Moloch will make him blast you, a few touches of
Death, getting totally digested by some purple worms and a few other
various deaths.

 Some of the other games mentioned could be finished without saving it's
just that it isn't easy or advisable.


 IMHO that there should be some way to ultimately kill the Wizard of
Yendor, it just isn't fair that he can keep coming back again and again.
Also is there any means in which you can do a touch of death ? It can be
done by the wizard and master liches so can it be gained by a player?


